From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@linux.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Drop git gc from the boringssl patch step

The patch step chains a repack onto the thing it is actually there to do:

    PATCH_COMMAND git apply ${patch_file} && git gc --aggressive

boringssl is fetched at --depth=1 into a build directory that is thrown away,
so there is nothing for an aggressive repack to save. It is housekeeping on a
tree with no history to keep.

It also fails. On a macOS runner:

    fatal: packfile .git/objects/pack/pack-4313fd03....pack cannot be mapped:
           Value too large to be stored in data type
    fatal: failed to run repack
    make[2]: *** [src/boringssl-stamp/boringssl-patch] Error 128

and because the stamp never lands, the half-prepared tree is what the compiler
then reads:

    crypto/fipsmodule/aes/aes.c:53:10: fatal error: cannot open file
      '.../crypto/fipsmodule/aes/internal.h': Illegal byte sequence

The second error is the one that gets reported, and it points at boringssl
rather than at the repack that caused it.

Removing the repack leaves the patch step doing only what it is named for. It
is in common/ rather than macos/ because the command has no build purpose on
any platform, not because the other two were observed to fail -- they were not.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Carried by firebase_ffi, where the set is maintained:
https://github.com/jwinarske/firebase_ffi/tree/main/packages/firebase_ffi/patches/firebase-cpp-sdk
---
--- a/cmake/external/boringssl.cmake
+++ b/cmake/external/boringssl.cmake
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ ExternalProject_Add(
     COMMAND git init boringssl
     COMMAND cd boringssl && git fetch --depth=1 https://github.com/google/boringssl.git ${boringssl_commit_tag} && git reset --hard FETCH_HEAD
 
-  PATCH_COMMAND git apply ${patch_file} && git gc --aggressive
+  PATCH_COMMAND git apply ${patch_file}
   PREFIX ${PROJECT_BINARY_DIR}
   CONFIGURE_COMMAND ""
   BUILD_COMMAND     ""
